### TITLE ###
TypingFiltersToSubsequenceMatches
### DESCRIPTION ###
Typing "av" narrows to avocado: the filter line appears and the non-matches
leave the list.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
apple
banana
avocado
### KEYS ###
"av"
enter
### SELECTED ###
avocado
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> apple
  banana
  avocado
--- frame 1 (a) ---
Pick
/a
> apple
  avocado
  banana
--- frame 2 (v) ---
Pick
/av
> avocado
--- frame 3 (enter) ---
Pick avocado

### TITLE ###
NoMatchesBlocksSubmit
### DESCRIPTION ###
Enter with an empty match set does nothing, so the script runs out of events and
the prompt ends canceled. The frame shows the no-matches hint rather than an
empty list a reader would have to interpret.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
apple
banana
### KEYS ###
"z"
enter
### SELECTED ###
<canceled>
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> apple
  banana
--- frame 1 (z) ---
Pick
/z
  (no matches - backspace to widen)
--- frame 2 (enter) ---
Pick
/z
  (no matches - backspace to widen)

### TITLE ###
CtrlUClearsTheFilter
### DESCRIPTION ###
Clearing the filter restores every option and puts the cursor back at the top,
so Enter selects the first option rather than the last match.
### PROMPT ###
Pick
### OPTIONS ###
apple
banana
avocado
### KEYS ###
"av"
ctrl-u
enter
### SELECTED ###
apple
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Pick
> apple
  banana
  avocado
--- frame 1 (a) ---
Pick
/a
> apple
  avocado
  banana
--- frame 2 (v) ---
Pick
/av
> avocado
--- frame 3 (ctrl-u) ---
Pick
> apple
  banana
  avocado
--- frame 4 (enter) ---
Pick apple
